    "summary": "Concrete ValueProviderResult enumeration is forced through an interface enumerator.",
    "explanation": "ValueProviderResult is a custom readonly struct used on model-binding request paths, but its public GetEnumerator returns IEnumerator<string>. Casting the StringValues struct to IEnumerable<string> boxes it, and the interface-shaped return prevents concrete foreach callers from using a value-type enumerator directly.",
    "snippet": "public IEnumerator<string> GetEnumerator()\n{\n    return ((IEnumerable<string>)Values).GetEnumerator();\n}",
    "suppressed": false
  },
